# STEMROBIN-182 N13 Modern Text Review FIRST

Verdict: **REVISE**. One substantive task-scope defect in exercise 181(a). All nine prose blocks and the other sixteen exercises pass this bounded text review. This FIRST decision is frozen for the exact candidate hashes below; no candidate was edited.

Review decision time: 2026-11-19T20:42:18Z.

## Finding

**[P2] Exercise 181(a) no longer unambiguously includes all nine table entries.**

File: `/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/stemrobin-182-resume/lemmadeck/.tmp/resume182-4-postaccount/n13-adapt/adapt/7a/modern-us-neutral/lessons/alg7-c1-s4-n13/exercises.template.json`

Exact affected JSON pointers: `/exercises/13/text` and `/exercises/13/lines/1`.

Source binding: `/exercises/13/pages = ["p0064#6", "p0065#1"]`. Immutable source wording introduces "太阳系九大行星" and then asks "把行星按照质量递增的顺序写出来". In that wording, the sorting task encompasses the nine listed entries.

The modern prefix instead introduces "原教材列出的太阳系九个天体", but subpart (a) still says "把行星按照质量递增的顺序写出来". The switch from nine celestial bodies in the prefix to planets in the command leaves the membership of the requested sorting set unclear. A reader can reasonably sort only a subset instead of all nine source entries. Historical-data attribution in the prefix does not resolve this noun mismatch.

Suggested minimal replacement for `/exercises/13/lines/1`:

```text
a) 把表中的九个天体按照质量递增的顺序写出来；
```

Suggested corresponding full `/exercises/13/text`:

```text
181. 下表保留了原教材列出的太阳系九个天体的质量数据：
a) 把表中的九个天体按照质量递增的顺序写出来；
b) 木星质量是地球质量的多少倍？
```

This restores the complete source task without asserting a modern nine-planet classification, deleting any source entry, changing a mass, or adding a solution. Keep subpart (b), `pages`, `figure_refs`, `figures`, source snapshots, and all numerical/math fields unchanged. Existing `changes` already includes `modernized`; no new mathematical correction or numeric-change record is called for.

