## Preservation and Boundaries

- Every target's `source_text` equals its corresponding embedded `source.data` text. All nine prose `source_refs` and all seventeen exercise `pages` arrays retain their source bindings, including 181's two-block binding.
- Exercise `number`, `source_number`, `group`, `group_id`, `figure_refs`, and `figures` match the source snapshot for every exercise. 182-184 remain in `复习题` / `g1`; 168-181 remain in `g0`.
- All authored exercise `lines` match `text` split on newlines. Cyrillic subpart labels were converted by sequence, not confused with similarly shaped Latin glyphs. No Cyrillic character remains in learner-facing prose/exercise `text`.
- Exercise 179 `/historical_entities/0` declares `苏联` with a `p0064#4`-bound reason; the term occurs in source and modern text. `БЭСМ-2` maps consistently to `BESM-2`. The visible E/C-shaped second model remains `EC-10-50`, with script ambiguity explicitly recorded in `authoring.record` and the declaration reason. This review makes no claim that source pixels establish Unicode identity, and does not substitute a researched model or erase the historical country.
- `/errata = []`; all `numeric_changes = []`. No formula correction, scientific-data replacement, modern demographic fact, added result, or new solving step was introduced.
- The table appears in lesson `figures` as a catalog entry, not as a prose figure block. Only exercise 181 references and display-lists it. Figure-template metadata agrees on its id. This is a text/ownership check only, not an image, table-cell, FigureSpec, or rendered-visibility approval.
- Authored prose flows from motivation to standard form, negative exponents, the general definition, and four worked examples. Complete statements and formulas remain readable. `/section_breaks = []` adds no unverified final-paragraph anchors. No renderer/prose-flow command was run and no final published paragraph count or viewport appearance is claimed.
- Existing worked examples are legitimate lesson teaching, not newly inserted exercise solutions. No learner-facing answer key, hidden grading field, HTML wrapper, source reference, or script-ambiguity note was added to the prose/exercise text. Author/source metadata was assessed as offline metadata, not claimed to be a tested client payload.

